<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!--
      Library manifest - intentionally declares no application attributes.

      BACKUP EXCLUSION: no manifest configuration is required by the consuming app.

      The software keystore is stored in Context.getNoBackupFilesDir(), which Android never
      includes in Auto Backup, cloud backup, or device-to-device transfer. That holds regardless
      of the app's android:allowBackup, android:fullBackupContent, or android:dataExtractionRules
      values, so the private key cannot leave the device through backup infrastructure even if the
      app opts into full backups.

      This replaces the previous approach of shipping backup_rules.xml / data_extraction_rules.xml
      for the app to reference. That approach could not be made reliable: each of
      android:fullBackupContent and android:dataExtractionRules accepts exactly one resource
      reference and nothing merges them, so if any other library (expo-secure-store, for example)
      or the app itself set either attribute, this module's exclusions were silently inactive. The
      no-backup directory needs no coordination between libraries, so both XML files were removed.

      Keys generated with useHardwareKey are held in the Android Keystore and are non-exportable,
      so they are not backup-eligible in the first place.
    -->
</manifest>
